- The sun is a circle of radius R whose center moves along the x-axis at height 0
  from left to right.
- Buildings are axis-aligned rectangles standing on the ground.
- We must find the last time (x-position of the sun center) such that the whole
  sunlight is blocked by the union of building silhouettes before sunset.

